s=A.a([A.cj(A.Z(A.a([A.vk(A.a5(20),A.wx("assets/images/logo.png",B.Mf,80,80),B.bl),B.L,A.f("\u0cad\u0cbe\u0cb0\u0ca4\u0cc0\u0caf\u0cae\u0ccd",o,o,o,o,A.k(o,o,$.av(),o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,22,o,o,B.E,o,o,!0,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o),o,o,o),A.f("Bharatheeyam \u2014 Vedic Astrology",o,o,o,o,A.k(o,o,$.ae(),o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,14,o,o,o,o,o,!0,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o),o,o,o),A.f("Version 1.0.1  \u2022  Open Source (AGPL-3.0)",o,o,o,o,A.k(o,o,$.ae(),o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,12,o,o,o,o,o,!0,o,o,o,o,o,o,o,o),o,o,o)],l),B.j,B.f,B.i,B.l),o,o),B.ak,A.iW("\u0cb2\u0cc6\u0c95\u0ccd\u0c95\u0cbe\u0c9a\u0cbe\u0cb0 \u0c8e\u0c82\u0c9c\u0cbf\u0ca8\u0ccd / Calculation Engine"),A.nl("All planetary positions are calculated using the Swiss Ephemeris \u2014 the world's most accurate astronomical positional engine, developed by Astrodienst AG (Z\xfcrich, Switzerland). It is accurate to sub-arcsecond precision and covers dates from 5400 BCE to 5400 CE.\n\nThe engine takes: birth date, time (in UTC), latitude, and longitude as input and computes precise sidereal planetary longitudes.",B.UQ,"Swiss Ephemeris (sweph)"),B.bx,A.iW("\u0c85\u0caf\u0ca8\u0cbe\u0c82\u0cb6 / Ayanamsa"),A.nl("The Swiss Ephemeris returns tropical (Western) longitudes. Vedic astrology uses the sidereal zodiac. The difference between tropical and sidereal is called Ayanamsa.\n\n\u2022 Lahiri (Chitrapaksha) \u2014 Official Indian government standard. Most widely used in India.\n\u2022 KP (Krishnamurti Paddhati) \u2014 A slightly different Ayanamsa used in KP astrology system.\n\u2022 Raman \u2014 Developed by B.V. Raman, another popular choice.\n\nSidereal Longitude = Tropical Longitude \u2212 Ayanamsa",B.Us,"Tropical \u2192 Sidereal Conversion"),B.bx,A.iW("\u0c95\u0cc1\u0c82\u0ca1\u0cb2\u0cbf / Birth Chart"),A.nl("After computing sidereal longitudes, the app places each planet (Sun, Moon, Mars, Mercury, Jupiter, Venus, Saturn, Rahu, Ketu, Mandi, and Gulika) into its Rashi (sign) and Nakshatra (lunar mansion).\n\n\ud83d\udcd0 House Cusps: Calculated using the Whole Sign house system \u2014 each house spans exactly one zodiac sign starting from the Lagna (Ascendant).\n\n\ud83c\udf19 Rahu & Ketu (Lunar Nodes): The app supports both True Node (actual astronomical position) and Mean Node (average position). Rahu and Ketu are always 180\xb0 apart.\n\n\u26a1 Mandi & Gulika: Calculated from the day's sunrise/sunset times and the weekday lord sequence using the classical Parashari method.",B.UL,"Graha Sphutas & House Cusps"),B.bx,A.iW("\u0caa\u0c82\u0c9a\u0cbe\u0c82\u0c97 / Panchanga"),A.nl("The Panchanga has five elements, each calculated from the Sun and Moon's positions:\n\n1. \u0cb5\u0cbe\u0cb0 (Vara) \u2014 Day of the week determined by the lord of the hour at sunrise. Each day has a ruling planet.\n\n2. \u0ca4\u0cbf\u0ca5\u0cbf (Tithi) \u2014 Lunar day. Calculated as the angular distance between Sun and Moon divided by 12\xb0. Each 12\xb0 = 1 Tithi. There are 30 Tithis in a lunar month.\n\n3. \u0ca8\u0c95\u0ccd\u0cb7\u0ca4\u0ccd\u0cb0 (Nakshatra) \u2014 Lunar mansion. The ecliptic is divided into 27 equal segments of 13\xb020' each. The Moon's position determines the current Nakshatra.\n\n4. \u0caf\u0ccb\u0c97 (Yoga) \u2014 Calculated by adding the sidereal longitudes of Sun + Moon, then dividing by 13\xb020'. There are 27 Yogas.\n\n5. \u0c95\u0cb0\u0ca3 (Karana) \u2014 Half a Tithi (6\xb0). There are 11 types of Karanas \u2014 4 fixed and 7 repeating.\n\n\u2600\ufe0f Sunrise & Sunset are calculated using the Swiss Ephemeris rise/set algorithm for the exact birth coordinates.",B.UK,"Five Limbs of the Hindu Calendar"),B.bx,A.iW("\u0caa\u0c82\u0c9a\u0cbe\u0c82\u0c97 \u0cb9\u0cac\u0ccd\u0cac\u0c97\u0cb3 \u0c86\u0ca7\u0cbe\u0cb0 / Panchanga Events Reference")],l)
